agent	Execute Claude Code CLI	2026-10-20T07:59:06.0085582Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgD8nAicT69p9jvvMSK4L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QPFUXo3E4Z9mAinxtoBH4B","name":"mcp__safeoutputs__add_comment","input":{"body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** not attempted: this is a style/feature request, and the issue gives no unexpected Black output to reproduce (the \"current style\" example is standard Black output).\n**Assessment:** The behaviour described is deliberate. Black wraps lines uniformly and puts one element per line (with trailing commas) when a bracketed expression doesn't fit, which keeps diffs small. The style docs also say configuration options are deliberately limited and rarely added, so a new `no-short-lines` / `min-line-length` option runs against that design. See \"How Black wraps lines\" in the current style docs: https://black.vercel.app/ (docs at black.readthedocs.io, `the_black_code_style/current_style`).\n**Next step:** Maintainers can weigh whether the proposal justifies a new option. Meanwhile, if you want to control the layout in specific places, removing the magic trailing comma lets Black collapse a collection that fits on one line.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: `R: not a bug` (or a decision on whether to accept a new option)</sub>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":956,"cache_read_input_tokens":48907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":956,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbc5102b-1b61-44e5-8f81-5c98d4b3ad80",